strings |id, value|

bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_af_cedilla_hint_differs_from_chrome_2026-11-28, 0, "After the Latin autohinter port, the cedilla of U+00E7 and U+00C7 is the one accent that still differs from Chrome 159 at 1x: about 7 mismatching px a glyph at 16 px Liberation Sans (rows 235..237 of the fixture: Chrome '361' / '37' / '674', engine '35' / '266' / '684'), 2 or 3 px at 10 px. Fixture: an absolutely positioned p of accented letters at 8..20 px, black on white; the other accented letters, the tilde letters, the ring of U+00C5, ! ? ^ _ ` ~ Q i j match (whole rows: base 120..540 mismatching px, port 0..16, all cedilla or run-end columns)."
    web_render_af_cedilla_hint_differs_from_chrome_2026-11-28, 1, "Not the cause, measured: FreeType 2.14's diacritic adjustment database (afadjust.c). FreeType 2.14 switches the blue alignment off below the base glyph for these two letters (AF_IGNORE_SMALL_BOTTOM / AF_IGNORE_CAPITAL_BOTTOM); its outline mismatches the Chrome capture just as much (6 of 12 px at 16 px), and Chrome has none of that database: the dot of an 8 px i sits against the stem (FreeType 2.14 lifts it 40/64 px) and FreeType 2.14's outlines of the accented letters mismatch Chrome by 4..21 px a glyph at 10..16 px where the port without the database matches."
    web_render_af_cedilla_hint_differs_from_chrome_2026-11-28, 2, "Open: which edge of the cedilla contour Chrome's hinter (skrifa) places differently. Check first whether the two glyphs are composites and, if so, how the component's points enter the hinter (order, rounding of the component offset), before looking at blue edges."

